[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Spice V2 - Independent Physical Consistency Audits

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Version 2.0, 2026-11-20. Ports the proven independent physical-audit concepts from v1 (CONS-*) into a clean, opt-in C++20 verification layer (v2/cpp/audit) and .NET result contract. Audits evaluate element-level conservation laws independently of solver matrices; passing checks confirm physical consistency within recorded tolerances, never global waveform accuracy or compact-model physical validity.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1. Opt-in independent physical checks

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-001
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Explicit bounded audit outcomes and opt-in execution
STATEMENT: >>>
Physical audits shall report passed, failed, or not_checked outcomes with SI discrepancy, effective tolerance, and an explicit reason when unavailable. Audits shall be selectable per run (default enabled in verification/test suites, opt-in during raw speed benchmarks) so unrequested audits never tax production solver throughput.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Test passed, failed, and not_checked transitions, nonfinite arithmetic rejection, and zero audit overhead when disabled in benchmark runs.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-002
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Independent DC KCL, voltage-constraint and power conservation
STATEMENT: >>>
The DC physical audit shall reconstruct element currents independently of assembled MNA matrices, verify KCL at every node including ground, verify ideal voltage/inductor/controlled-voltage constraints in voltage units, and verify passive-sign power conservation including any explicit Gmin regularization.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Perturb a single node voltage or branch current and confirm independent KCL, voltage-constraint, and power checks detect the defect.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: AUDIT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-003
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Independent linear AC complex current and power balance
STATEMENT: >>>
For supported small-signal AC points, the audit shall independently verify complex KCL, complex source constraints, and complex power balance (Tellegen's theorem) across real and imaginary components.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Exercise RC, RLC, and controlled-source AC solutions with complex excitations and verify perturbation detection.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: AUDIT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-004
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Discrete transient step conservation and dissipation
STATEMENT: >>>
For supported fixed or accepted backward-Euler and trapezoidal steps, the transient audit shall independently check companion currents, inductor voltages, KCL, source constraints, and discrete energy balance (explicitly accounting for backward-Euler numerical dissipation) while retaining worst normalized discrepancies with bounded memory.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Verify RC/RLC transient steps and confirm perturbed states or missing dissipation terms fail the audit.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: AUDIT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-005
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Explicit non-claims on global accuracy
STATEMENT: >>>
Audit reports shall explicitly mark global continuous-time accuracy as not_checked and distinguish physical step consistency from timestep-refinement comparison and independent oracle agreement.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Inspect serialized ResultManifest audit sections and confirm global_accuracy stays explicitly not_checked.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: AUDIT-001

[[/SECTION]]
